<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>PO Light — Wiring Diagram &amp; Troubleshooting Guide</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root{
    --bg:#12151a; --panel:#1a1f26; --line:#2c333d; --text:#e6eaee; --muted:#8b96a3;
    --amber:#e8a33d; --coral:#e8654f; --teal:#46b8a6; --gray:#3a4250; --purple:#a888e0;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:24px 12px 60px;}
  h1{font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-size:19px;margin:0 0 6px;text-align:center;}
  h2{font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-size:14.5px;margin:36px 0 4px;text-align:left;width:100%;max-width:720px;color:var(--purple);}
  h3{font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-size:13px;margin:18px 0 8px;text-align:left;width:100%;max-width:720px;color:var(--amber);}
  .sub{color:var(--muted);font-size:11.5px;width:100%;max-width:720px;text-align:left;margin:0 0 12px;line-height:1.6;}
  p.lead{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;text-align:center;max-width:580px;margin:0 0 6px;line-height:1.6;}
  .disclaimer{width:100%;max-width:720px;margin:14px 0 6px;padding:10px 14px;background:#241a17;border:1px solid #4a2e24;border-radius:6px;color:#e8a08f;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.6;}
  .method{width:100%;max-width:720px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:16px 18px;margin-top:8px;}
  .method ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.9;color:var(--text);}
  .method li b{color:var(--amber);}
  svg{width:100%;max-width:720px;height:auto;background:var(--bg);}
  .rail{stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.5;}
  .wire{stroke:var(--muted);stroke-width:1.3;fill:none;}
  .sym{stroke:var(--text);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;}
  .symfill{fill:var(--panel);stroke:var(--text);stroke-width:1.2;}
  .th{font-family:'Space Grotesk',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:12.5px;fill:var(--text);}
  .ts{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;fill:var(--muted);}
  .tsAmber{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;fill:var(--amber);}
  .tsCut{font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;fill:var(--coral);}

  table{width:100%;max-width:720px;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:11px;margin-top:6px;}
  th,td{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:8px 9px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;line-height:1.5;}
  th{background:var(--panel);color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;font-size:10.5px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.03em;}
  td.name{color:var(--amber);font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;}
  tr.cut td{color:#e8a08f;}
  .badge{display:inline-block;font-size:9.5px;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:10px;background:#4a2e24;color:#e8a08f;margin-left:6px;letter-spacing:.02em;}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>PO light — wiring diagram &amp; troubleshooting guide</h1>
<p class="lead">Built from your engineering prints and physical wire tags: the three wiring diagram sheets, plus contact-by-contact continuity and voltage checks for every point in the chain.</p>
<div class="disclaimer"><b>Verify before use:</b> assembled from photos and prints across our conversation, not an original as-built drawing. Cross-check against the physical panel before doing any work.</div>

<!-- ============ SHEET 1 ============ -->
<h2>Sheet 1 — Power supervision logic</h2>
<div class="sub">XPR relaxed (back contact closed) = AC present → energizes both POR coils → both front contacts pass in series → PO lamp lit.</div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 660 380" role="img">
<title>Power supervision ladder logic diagram</title>
<desc>Two-rail ladder logic: the coil rung shows XPR's normally closed contact at terminal 21 feeding both the 1-POR and 2-POR relay coils in parallel, strapped together at terminal 11. The contact rung shows the 1-POR and 2-POR front contacts at terminal 5 in series, feeding the POK wire to WAGO terminal 20 plus and the PO lamp.</desc>

<line class="rail" x1="60" y1="50" x2="60" y2="330"/>
<text class="th" x="60" y="34" text-anchor="middle">MB / AA5+</text>
<line class="rail" x1="600" y1="50" x2="600" y2="330"/>
<text class="th" x="600" y="34" text-anchor="middle">MN return</text>

<line class="wire" x1="60" y1="110" x2="150" y2="110"/>
